# The suite's time budget on CI, judged per split share at the recorded list's
# runner speed: each job and the share total, divided by the share's runner
# factor (the median, over jobs recorded in Distribution/tests/longest-first with a
# measurable recorded time of at least 2 s, of observed/recorded seconds),
# must stay within per-job-seconds and total-job-seconds. scripts/test.sh
# compares each CI split's times that way, and a breach fails that split
# naming observed time, factor and time at recorded speed; a local run is not
# judged. The per-check ceiling remains 64: the existing native-substitute
# split in 58ca884b9 fixes that check's cost without raising its limit.
# The aggregate allowance repacks four shares into three: ceil(694×4/3)=926,
# preserving the former per-run allowance apart from integer rounding.
# Prior calibration was twelve retained main runs 40834521203 … 41004369454
# plus 41000649845/1: largest share 577.5×1.2→694, job 52.7×1.2→64.
# Evidence and limits: docs/maintainer/ci-budget-calibration.md.
# Raising either number is reviewed, not a way to make a slow change pass.
# Whole-run solo/overlap evidence still decides whether this packing stays.
# Check recent trunk times with `bash scripts/ci-test-times.sh`
# (Distribution/tests/time-budget.md).
per-job-seconds=64
total-job-seconds=926
